  "Question": "Each day Maria must work \\(8\\) hours. This does not include the \\(45\\) minutes she takes for lunch. If she begins working at \\(7{:}25\\) A.M. and takes her lunch break at noon, then her working day will end at",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(3{:}40\\) P.M.",
    "B": "\\(3{:}55\\) P.M.",
    "C": "\\(4{:}10\\) P.M.",
    "D": "\\(4{:}25\\) P.M.",
    "E": "\\(4{:}40\\) P.M."
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "The lunch break does not count toward Maria's \\(8\\) hours of work, so the time from starting to finishing is \\(8\\) hours \\(45\\) minutes.\n\nStarting at \\(7{:}25\\) A.M., adding \\(8\\) hours brings us to \\(3{:}25\\) P.M. Adding the lunch break gives \\(25+45=70\\) minutes past \\(3\\). Since \\(70\\) minutes equals \\(1\\) hour \\(10\\) minutes, Maria finishes at \\(\\boxed{4{:}10\\text{ P.M.}}\\), choice C.",
